 gardens; mariachi afternoon","bookable_category":"private trajinera tour","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.viator.com/tours/Mexico-City/Private-Tour-in-Trajinera-through-the-Canals-of-Xochimilco/d628-289853P13 — Accessed 2026-07-05","timing":"Oct 31","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","blurb":"colorful boats poled through UNESCO canals + floating gardens; mariachi afternoon","when":"Oct 31","commission":"affiliate ~8% (Viator private) or DMC","accessed":"2026-07-05","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture","romance"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","culture":"evidenced","entertainment":"destination","romance":"primary"},"commission_pct_low":8,"commission_pct_high":8,"commission_lane":["DMC","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"Sunday Paseo de la Reforma (Muévete en Bici)","si_tag":"Romance & Honeymoons","status":"live","hook":"the grand boulevard closes to cars Sunday mornings for cyclists + walkers","bookable_category":"bike tour / self-guided","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.casagoliana.com/blog/best-time-to-visit-mexico-city/ — Accessed 2026-07-05","timing":"Oct 31","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","blurb":"the grand boulevard closes to cars Sunday mornings for cyclists + walkers","when":"Oct 31","commission":"affiliate","accessed":"2026-07-05","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["romance"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","culture":"destination","entertainment":"destination","romance":"primary"},"commission_lane":["affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Jacaranda-season Roma-Condesa stroll + rooftop dinner","si_tag":"Romance & Honeymoons","status":"live","hook":"Mar–Apr purple canopies over the prettiest neighborhoods + Polanco rooftop","bookable_category":"hotel + private guide + reservation","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.casagoliana.com/blog/best-time-to-visit-mexico-city/ — Accessed 2026-07-05","timing":"Oct 31","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","blurb":"Mar–Apr purple canopies over the prettiest neighborhoods + Polanco rooftop","when":"Oct 31","commission":"DMC (Fora lane)","accessed":"2026-07-05","wells":["stay","eat","activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culinary","romance"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"evidenced","culture":"destination","entertainment":"destination","romance":"primary"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"Will the altitude affect me?","a":"It can for the first day or two. The city sits at **~2,240 m (7,349 ft)** — roughly 25% less oxygen than sea level — and most travelers need **24–72 hours** to acclimate; mild headache, fatigue and breathlessness are common on arrival from sea level and pass with rest, hydration and easing off alcohol on day one. Fitness and age do not predict susceptibility.","source":"nomadoc.com.mx, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is Mexico City good for a romantic city break?","a":"Strongly — it''s the one live-launch SI that genuinely fits an inland capital. The romance lane is Polanco/Reforma luxe: the St. Regis atop the **31-story Torre Libertad**, the Sofitel''s **38th-floor pool**, rooftop dining, and the March–April jacaranda bloom that turns Roma-Condesa purple.","source":"blacklane.com / casagoliana.com, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What are the must-see culture sites, and is Teotihuacán worth it?","a":"Yes — the heritage circuit runs from the Museo Nacional de Antropología (the Aztec Sun Stone) and Templo Mayor beneath the Zócalo out to Teotihuacán, ~50 km northeast, best at dawn by private balloon (**$150–$300 USD**). It''s the single greatest day-trip from the city.","source":"mexicocity-tours.com, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Do I need reservations for Pujol and the top restaurants?","a":"Yes — book weeks ahead. Pujol (top-5 on Latin America''s 50 Best) and Quintonil sell their tasting menus out well in advance, and Casa Luis Barragán tickets release Tuesdays at noon CDMX time and sell out within minutes. Lock the marquee tables the moment the trip is confirmed.","source":"theinfatuation.com, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"Where''s the best nightlife and cocktail scene?","a":"Roma-Condesa. Licorería Limantour was named **Best Bar in North America in 2022 and 2023**, and the surrounding streets hold the city''s densest cluster of cocktail bars, mezcalerías and traditional pulquerías — best done as a guided crawl.","source":"mezcalistas.com, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"entertainment","si_fold_note":"folded from the retired `nightlife` slug into Global Live Entertainment 2026-08-23; the content is kept, the retired slug is not"},{"q":"When is Día de Muertos, and can I see the parade?","a":"Oct 31–Nov 2, with the Grand Parade on ~Nov 1 running **~6 km** from Chapultepec down Reforma to the Zócalo — the biggest live-culture moment of the CDMX year. Parade-corridor hotels (Centro/Reforma) tighten sharply through October, so book weeks out.","source":"casagoliana.com, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"entertainment"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Mexico City (CDMX) Travel Guide 2026 — Culture, Food & Día de Muertos | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Plan a Mexico City trip with TravelWell.World: when to go (Día de Muertos, jacaranda season), where to stay (Four Seasons to Roma villas), food and culture jewels, altitude and safety — all bookable.","slug":"mexico-city-mexico","primary_keyword":"Mexico City travel guide","long_tail":["best time to visit Mexico City","Día de Muertos Mexico City 2026","Mexico City altitude sickness","luxury hotels Polanco","Teotihuacán balloon day trip","Roma Condesa restaurants"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-05","search_language":"en + es-MX","local_keywords":["qué hacer en CDMX","Día de Muertos Ciudad de México","mejores restaurantes Roma Condesa","hoteles de lujo Polanco","globo aerostático Teotihuacán","mejor época para visitar la Ciudad de México"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-07-05","last_verified_basis":"source_verified","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-20T14:49:02Z","source_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}]}},"booking":{"advisory_updated":"2026-08-20","advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"romance","status":"live"},{"si":"culture","status":"future"},{"si":"culinary","status":"future"},{"si":"entertainment","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Four Seasons Hotel Mexico City","why_ultra":"hacienda-style courtyard-oasis on Reforma; 240 rooms/40 suites; FS service benchmark","earning":"Four Seasons Preferred Partner / Virtuoso via host","virtuoso_value_add":"upgrade + daily breakfast + $100 credit + early/late (verify)","mor":"hotel/chain","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"St. Regis Mexico City","why_ultra":"31-story Torre Libertad; 189 rooms; butler service; best high-floor Reforma views","earning":"Marriott STARS/Luxury via host (Fora)","virtuoso_value_add":"STARS amenity: credit + upgrade + breakfast","mor":"hotel/chain","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Las Alcobas (Luxury Collection, Polanco)","why_ultra":"Yabu Pushelberg 35-room jewel-box; butler; Anatol + Dulce","earning":"Marriott Luxury STARS/Luminous via host (Fora)","virtuoso_value_add":"STARS amenity","mor":"hotel/chain","tier":"premier-ultra"},{"name":"Sofitel Mexico City Reforma","why_ultra":"French-luxe, 38th-floor pool over the city; 275+56 suites","earning":"Accor Sofitel preferred / Virtuoso via host (Fora)","virtuoso_value_add":"preferred-partner amenity","mor":"hotel/chain","tier":"premier-luxury"},{"name":"Casa Polanco","why_ultra":"restored 1930s aristocratic residence; villa-like intimacy w/ hotel service","earning":"verify Virtuoso/preferred membership at booking","virtuoso_value_add":"TBD per program","mor":"hotel","tier":"premier-ultra"},{"name":"Pug Seal boutiques (Polanco)","why_ultra":"tiny art-filled design micro-hotels for boutique-over-grand ultra travelers","earning":"verify host/preferred program","virtuoso_value_add":"TBD","mor":"hotel","tier":"premier"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-05","hero":{"query":"Mexico City (CDMX), Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":19.4326,"lng":-99.1332},"orbit":[{"id":"teotihuacan-mexico","jewels":7,"si":["culture"]}],"orbit_country":["akumal-mexico","bacalar-mexico","balandra-beach-mexico","cabo-pulmo-mexico","cabo-san-lucas-mexico","calakmul-mexico","campeche-city-mexico","cancun-mexico","careyes-mexico","celestun-mexico","chapala-ajijic-mexico","chichen-itza-mexico","coba-mexico","costalegre-mexico","cozumel-mexico","east-cape-mexico","ensenada-mexico","espiritu-santo-island-mexico","guadalajara-mexico","guanajuato-city-mexico","holbox-mexico","huatulco-mexico","isla-contoy-mexico","isla-mujeres-mexico","izamal-mexico","la-paz-mexico","loreto-mexico","los-barriles-mexico","magdalena-bay-mexico","mahahual-mexico","mazamitla-mexico","merida-mexico","oaxaca-city-mexico","palenque-mexico","playa-del-carmen-mexico","puerto-aventuras-mexico","puerto-morelos-mexico","puerto-vallarta-mexico","punta-mita-mexico","rio-lagartos-mexico","san-cristobal-de-las-casas-mexico","san-jose-del-cabo-mexico","san-miguel-de-allende-mexico","san-sebastian-del-oeste-mexico","sayulita-mexico","sian-kaan-mexico","tlaquepaque-mexico","todos-santos-mexico","tulum-mexico","uxmal-mexico","valladolid-mexico","valle-de-guadalupe-mexico","puerto-escondido-mexico"]}'::jsonb, 70),
  ('monteverde-costa-rica', '10S', 'Monteverde', 'Costa Rica', 'The original cloud forest', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Costa Rica', '{"expedition","wildlife","romance"}', '{}', '{"essential","premier","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Birthplace of the commercial canopy zipline; Selvatura runs 13 ziplines incl. a 1 km line, 15 platforms, Tarzan swing, and 8 hanging bridges (51-170 m long, 12-60 m high).","Cloud forest protects 400+ bird species (resplendent quetzal, three-wattled bellbird), 2,500+ plants incl. 500+ orchids, 100+ mammals.","Three reserves: Monteverde Cloud Forest ($25, 7AM-4PM), Santa Elena (quieter, great quetzals), Curi-Cancha (least crowded, top birding).","Resplendent quetzal breeds Feb-Jun (peak Mar-Apr), best viewed 6-9 AM on wild-avocado trees.","Highland ~1,400 m; ~3-4 hr from SJO with a rough, partly-unpaved final mountain road; dengue risk low at elevation."],"safety":{"emergency":"911","nearest_clinic":"Santa Elena local clinics (minor/first response)","major_trauma":"San Jose hospitals (CIMA, Clinica Biblica), ~3-4 hr by road; air/ground evac pathway","advisory_reason":"Crime (petty nationwide; some violent crime, concentrated in specific San Jose neighborhoods)","advisory_issued":"2026-04-02","standard_caution":"No valuables in parked rental cars; registered operators; daylight driving on mountain road","activity_hazards":["zipline/canopy operator certification + harness/brakes + weight limits","mountain-road fog + unpaved sections (4WD, daylight)","night-walk footing + vipers (guided only)","wet suspension-bridge decking + heights"],"book_enabled":true,"air_access_verified":"SJO (Juan Santamaria) ~3-4 hr road; note rough/partly-unpaved access road","water":"Tap water generally potable including Monteverde area; bottled optional for sensitive travelers","dengue":"Low at ~1,400 m highland elevation; use repellent","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/costa-rica","read":"2026-08-20T14:54:18Z","page_updated":"2026-05-19T11:42:25+01:00","source_country":"costa-rica","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely"},"timing":{"national_dry_peak":"mid-December to April","holiday_hard_peak":"late December","quetzal_breeding":"February to June/July, peak March-April","green_secret_season":"May-June (low crowds, birding-rich, misty year-round)","wettest_month":"October","curve_start_dry":"early-mid December","curve_start_quetzal":"early February","fire_date":"late November (~Nov 20-27) for dry/holiday; mid-late January (~Jan 20-27) for quetzal-birding","booking_lead":"60-90 days peak; 2-4 weeks green season","note":"misty year-round; peak demand != peak experience; sharpen on live tracking"},"jewels":[{"name":"Selvatura Park canopy + bridges","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.selvatura.com/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"expedition","when":"year-round","commission":"Activities-Well direct or DMC bundle","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"primary","romance":"destination","wildlife":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC","bundle"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Sky Adventures (SkyTram/SkyTrek/SkyWalk)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://eternalarrival.com/ziplining-in-monteverde-canopy-tours/","si":"expedition","commission":"Activities-Well / DMC","wells":["move"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"primary","romance":"destination","wildlife":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"100% Aventura (Superman ziplines)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://mytanfeet.com/activities/100-aventura-monteverde/","si":"expedition","commission":"Activities-Well / DMC","well