"expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"primary","romance":"destination"},"commission_lane":["guide"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Santiago Matatlan mezcal route","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.oaxaca-mio.com/mezcalesdeoaxaca/matatlan.htm","timing":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","commission":"guided mezcal-route tour (DMC/Viator); bottles non-commissionable","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"primary","romance":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC","guide"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"El Tule (world''s widest tree)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://culturestraveled.com/hierve-el-agua-oaxaca/","timing":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"At Santa María del Tule, ~20 minutes from the city","si":"expedition","blurb":"At Santa María del Tule, ~20 minutes from the city","when":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","commission":"bundled into valley-circuit tour","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"primary","romance":"destination"},"commission_lane":["bundle"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Teotitlan del Valle weavers","si_tag":"romance","tier":"premier","source":"https://brokenbootstravel.com/the-travelers-guide-to-teotitlan-del-valle/","timing":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","when":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","commission":"private artisan-village tour (DMC); rug purchases direct-to-artisan","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["romance"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"destination","romance":"primary"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"San Bartolo Coyotepec black pottery","si_tag":"romance","tier":"essential","source":"https://theculturetrip.com/north-america/mexico/articles/a-tour-of-oaxacas-best-markets","timing":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","when":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","commission":"south-valley artisan tour (DMC)","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["romance"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"destination","romance":"primary"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Alebrijes at San Martin Tilcajete","si_tag":"romance","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.fiestamericanatravelty.com/en/grand-fiesta-americana/hotels/grand-fiesta-americana-oaxaca","timing":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","when":"Dia de Muertos Oct 31–Nov 2","commission":"artisan-workshop tour + hotel alebrije programming","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["romance"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"destination","romance":"primary"},"commission_lane":["hotel"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for?","a":"Terrain and high-proof spirits, not crime. The city is a mild **~1,555 m** (light first-day breathlessness at most); the genuine hazards are Hierve el Agua''s cliff-edge footing above a canyon and the mezcal route — high-proof tastings plus rural highway driving mean you take a driver or DMC, never self-drive after tasting.","source":"oaxacalife.com, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"When is Día de Muertos, and how far ahead do I book?","a":"Oct 31–Nov 2, and it''s the longest lead time in the inland catalog: book **4–8 months ahead** (5–6 months / May–June is the sweet spot). Walkable-Centro rooms are ~95% booked by early September and rates run **2–3× normal** ($150–250 USD/night).","source":"mexicotravelandleisure.com / wheregoesrose.com, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Is Oaxaca really a top food destination?","a":"Yes — it''s widely regarded as one of the world''s great food capitals. The \"seven moles,\" market-to-table cooking schools (Casa Crespo), and the mezcal terroir of Santiago Matatlán (~45 minutes southeast, the World Capital of Mezcal) are destination-defining reasons to go.","source":"oaxaca-mio.com, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"Is Hierve el Agua worth it — and will it be open?","a":"Worth it, but verify first. The petrified mineral \"waterfalls\" and clifftop spring-fed pools sit 70 km east near Mitla, but the site sees **periodic community-dispute closures clustering June–October** — always confirm it''s open the week before, and keep a Mitla + Tlacolula fallback ready.","source":"mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is Oaxaca good for couples?","a":"Yes — a slow, sensory, non-beach romance. Boutique casonas and the ex-convent (1576) Quinta Real, mezcal-tasting date nights, and the artisan-village shopping ritual (Teotitlán weaving, rugs $75–$500; San Bartolo black pottery; alebrijes) make the case.","source":"caminoreal.com / brokenbootstravel.com, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"romance"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Oaxaca City & the Central Valleys, Mexico — UNESCO, Mezcal, Dia de Muertos & Monte Alban | TravelWell.World","search_language":["en","es-MX"],"local_keywords":["Dia de Muertos Oaxaca","que hacer en Oaxaca","ruta del mezcal","Guelaguetza fechas","Monte Alban precio entrada","Hierve el Agua abierto","hoteles boutique Oaxaca centro","Noche de Rabanos"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-05","attribution":{"