 of road 45D."},{"name":"The state of Sinaloa","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán","road 32 between El Fuerte and Los Mochis","the 15D federal toll road running the length of the state","the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis and El Fuerte, and the towns immediately on it"]},{"name":"The state of Tamaulipas","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo via federal toll road 85D from Monterrey","federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad Victoria and Magueyes","the area of Tamaulipas south of those highways"]},{"name":"The state of Zacatecas","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"In Guanajuato: the areas south-west of road 45D","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D. (San Miguel de Allende and Guanajuato City sit outside this area.)"},{"name":"The state of Michoacán","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Morelia via federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43","toll road 48D between Morelia and its airport","the town of Pátzcuaro via toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips on Lake Pátzcuaro","Federal Highway 15D"]},{"name":"In Jalisco: the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the Colima border","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"Thirty-nine named municipalities, including Autlán de Navarro, Sayula, Tapalpa, Cocula and Villa Corona — the advisory lists each by name."},{"name":"In Jalisco: eleven northern municipalities","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"Bolaños, Chimaltitán, Colotlán, Hostotipaquillo, Huejúcar, Huequilla el Alto, Mezquitic, San Martín de Bolaños, Santa María de los Ángeles, Totatiche and Villa Guerrero."},{"name":"The state of Colima","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Manzanillo by sea, or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport","direct travel via road 200 from that airport to Manzanillo"]},{"name":"The state of Guerrero, including the city of Acapulco","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air"]},{"name":"Within 40km of the Guatemalan border, from the Pacific Coast up to and including the Gracias a Dios crossing","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"Federal Highway 199 between Rancho Nuevo, outside San Cristóbal de las Casas, and the Chancalá junction outside Palenque","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"The restriction is the highway segment, not the towns at either end."}]},"timing":{"peak":"Nov–Apr (dry season, jungle passable, waterfalls turquoise)","inflection":"early–mid September","fire_date":"late August (curve-start − 1–2 weeks)","off_season_specials":"May–Oct rainy — brown water, muddy roads, higher road risk"},"jewels":[{"name":"Temple of the Inscriptions + Pakal''s pyramid","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://mayaruins.com/palenque/a1_223.html","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"the anchor. Tomb descent closed since ~2004; regalia at the site museum","si":"culture","blurb":"the anchor. Tomb descent closed since ~2004; regalia at the site museum","when":"year-round","commission":"guided-tour DMC/affiliate (admission non-commissionable)","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"primary","expedition":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC","affiliate","guide"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"The Palace + observation tower","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/palenque-ruins-guide/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"the four-story tower is Palenque''s signature silhouette; the Palace complex is the civic heart of the site","si":"culture","blurb":"the four-story tower is Palenque''s signature silhouette; the Palace complex is the civic heart of the site","when":"year-round","commission":"guided-tour affiliate","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"primary","expedition":"destination"},"commission_lane":["affiliate","guide"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Site Museum + Pakal reconstructed tomb exhibit","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://mayaruins.com/palenque/a1_223.html","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","when":"year-round","commission":"bundled admission (non-commissionable)","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"primary","expedition":"destination"},"commission_lane":["bundle"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Bonampak murals (~792 AD)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.viator.com/tours/Palenque/Tour-Bonampak-and-Yaxchilan/d23479-30922P9","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"best-preserved Classic Maya murals on Earth, full-color three-room cycle","si":"culture","blurb":"best-preserved Classic Maya murals on Earth, full-color three-room cycle","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"full-day DMC tour","wells":["activities","stay"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"primary","expedition":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Yaxchilán by Usumacinta riverboat","si_tag":"culture","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.viator.com/tours/Palenque/Tour-Bonampak-and-Yaxchilan/d23479-30922P9","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Usumacinta motorboat into the Lacandón, ruins the road cannot reach","si":"culture","blurb":"Usumacinta motorboat into the Lacandón, ruins the road cannot reach","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"licensed river-tour DMC (border-verify)","wells":["move","activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"primary","expedition":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Agua Azul cascades","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.viator.com/tours/Palenque/Agua-Azul-and-Misol-Ha/d23479-30922P10","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"waterfall day-tour affiliate","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"destination","expedition":"primary"},"commission_lane":["affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Misol-Ha waterfall (Predator site)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/things-to-do-in-palenque/","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"day-tour affiliate","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"destination","expedition":"primary"},"commission_lane":["affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Roberto Barrios cascades","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://nomadearthcatalog.com/cascadas-roberto-barrios/","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"five off-the-beaten-track falls, turquoise pools, natural 10 m slide, ~45 min south, entry ~30 MXN","si":"expedition","blurb":"five off-the-beaten-track falls, turquoise pools, natural 10 m slide, ~45 min south, entry ~30 MXN","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"dedicated day-tour affiliate","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"destination","expedition":"primary"},"commission_lane":["affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Howler-monkey jungle canopy (dawn ruins)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.timetravelturtle.com/mexico/visit-palenque/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"the sound that defines dawn at Palenque; the ruins double as a wildlife encounter","si":"expedition","blurb":"the sound that defines dawn at Palenque; the ruins double as a wildlife encounter","when":"year-round","commission":"guided dawn tour upsell","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture","expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"evidenced","expedition":"primary"},"commission_lane":["guide"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Lacandón Jungle multi-day expedition","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"premier","source":"https://mayantourstravel.com/tours/the-amazing-lacandon-jungle-groups/","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"deep-forest circuit combining Bonampak, Yaxchilán and river camps","si":"expedition","blurb":"deep-forest circuit combining Bonampak, Yaxchilán and river camps","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"multi-day DMC","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"destination","expedition":"primary"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for — is the road dangerous?","a":"The road is the risk, not the ruins. The overland San Cristóbal↔Palenque highway via Ocosingo (Chilón) has a documented armed-robbery history — one reported incident had ~18 men with assault rifles set a roadblock and rob a line of tourist vehicles, with the worst incidents after dark. The rule is daytime-only, guided/convoy transfer, no self-drive, and the safer, longer Villahermosa toll-road approach where possible.","source":"mexiconewsdaily.com / jeniastraveldiaries.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"How remote is medical care from Palenque?","a":"Genuinely remote — plan for it. Palenque is a small town with limited advanced care; serious trauma routes to Villahermosa or Tuxtla Gutiérrez, with air evacuation to Mexico City for anything major. Bonampak, Yaxchilán and the deep-jungle waterfalls are hours from a hospital, so carry evacuation insurance — and note dengue is present year-round with malaria risk in rural Chiapas.","source":"mexiconewsdaily.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What will I see at the Palenque ruins?","a":"A Maya city the rainforest never fully released: the Temple of the Inscriptions rising over Pakal the Great''s tomb, and the four-story observation tower of the Palace, its civic heart. The tomb chamber itself has been closed to descent since ~2004 to protect it, so you see the pyramid and Pakal''s regalia at the site museum, not the crypt. Go at the 8 AM opening before the jungle heat.","source":"mayaruins.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"What are the Palenque waterfalls, and when should I go?","a":"Three systems within reach: Agua Azul''s 500+ turquoise cascades over ~6 km, the ~35 m Misol-Ha plunge with a walk-behind grotto, and the quieter Roberto Barrios falls with a natural rock slide (~45 min south, entry ~30 MXN). Come November–April, when the mineral-rich water runs brilliant turquoise; in the May–October rains sediment turns Agua Azul brown. Swim only in marked zones — currents are strong.","source":"mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Can I visit Bonampak and Yaxchilán?","a":"Yes, as a full-day guided expedition. Bonampak holds the best-preserved Classic Maya murals in existence (~792 AD), and Yaxchilán is reachable only by motorboat on the Usumacinta River, the water border with Guatemala. Go with a licensed operator, not an ad-hoc boatman, verify current border and security conditions before booking, and travel by daylight with life vests.","source":"viator.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Palenque, Mexico: Jungle Maya Ruins, Waterfalls & Safe Travel Guide (2026) | TravelWell","search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["ruinas de Palenque","Agua Azul Chiapas","Misol-Ha","Yaxchilán Bonampak","cascadas Roberto Barrios","Templo de las Inscripciones Pakal","cómo llegar a Palenque desde Villahermosa"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","primary_keyword":"Palenque","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-08-20","last_verified_basis":"safety.fcdo.read","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-20T14:49:02Z","source_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}]},"content_freshness":"2026-07-07"},"booking":{"advisory_updated":"2026-08-20","advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"culture","status":"live"},{"si":"expedition","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Chan-Kah Resort Village","tier":"premier","mor":"bedbank/direct","earning":"modest — upper-mid ADR, not luxury; live"},{"name":"Boutique Quinta Chanabnal","tier":"premier","mor":"advisor/direct","earning":"modest"},{"name":"Piedra de Agua Palenque","tier":"comfort","mor":"verify","earning":"to verify"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Palenque, Mexico, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":17.484,"lng":-92.046},"orbit":[{"id":"san-cristo