"affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Garifuna Coast — Hopkins day trip","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","tier":"essential","hook":"Drumming, culture and beaches of the Garifuna village of Hopkins.","bookable_category":"cultural day trip","source":"https://www.hamanasi.com/belize-vacation/cockscomb-jaguar-preserve-tour/","timing":"late-Dec-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"Drumming, culture and beaches of the Garifuna village of Hopkins.","when":"late-Dec-Apr","commission":"DMC AOR / affiliate","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"primary","diveglobal":"destination","expedition":"destination","liveaboard":"destination","ocean":"destination","wildlife":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Flats fly-fishing (permit / bonefish / tarpon)","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures","status":"future","tier":"premier","hook":"World-class permit water on the southern flats, year-round.","bookable_category":"guided fly-fishing","source":"https://www.jmbelizetravel.com/placencia-sea-tours/","timing":"late-Dec-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"ocean","blurb":"World-class permit water on the southern flats, year-round.","when":"late-Dec-Apr","commission":"fishing-lodge/guide direct; affiliate on packaged trips","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["ocean"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"destination","diveglobal":"destination","expedition":"destination","liveaboard":"destination","ocean":"primary","wildlife":"destination"},"commission_lane":["package","affiliate","hotel","guide"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Placencia sidewalk + fishing village","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","tier":"essential","hook":"The famous narrow sidewalk, seafood shacks and end-of-peninsula soul.","bookable_category":"self-guided","source":"https://chabilmarvillas.com/","timing":"late-Dec-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"The famous narrow sidewalk, seafood shacks and end-of-peninsula soul.","when":"late-Dec-Apr","commission":"none (drives F&B + lodging attach)","wells":["stay","activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"primary","diveglobal":"destination","expedition":"destination","liveaboard":"destination","ocean":"destination","wildlife":"destination"},"commission_lane":["none"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is Placencia good for a honeymoon or wedding?","a":"Yes — it is Belize''s most credible mainland resort/romance market, with real luxury-to-ultra range. Naïa Resort & Spa (39 beach houses + treetop villas on 224 private acres, mile of beach, from ~US$380/night) and SLH-member Itz''ana anchor the beachfront, plus true private-island elopements offshore. The peninsula earns both the wedding and the dive log.","source":"naiaresortandspa.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"When can you swim with whale sharks in Placencia?","a":"Around the Mar–Jun full moons at Gladden Spit — the one place on the planet where whale-shark arrival is \"reasonably predictable.\" 2026 full moons are Mar 14, Apr 13, May 12 and Jun 11, with windows ~2 days before to ~10 days after; April and May fill first, so serious divers book three to four months ahead. Encounters are not guaranteed — you''re buying the window.","source":"splashbelize.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"liveaboard"},{"q":"What wildlife can you see near Placencia?","a":"Two flagship day trips. The Monkey River eco-tour (a ~45-min coastal boat run then a river cruise) carries you into black-howler-monkey habitat with crocodiles, iguanas, toucans and manatees on the return; and the Cockscomb Basin — the world''s first jaguar preserve, 128,000 acres, est. 1986 — is a half-day inland via Maya Center.","source":"blueturtleplacencia.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Does Placencia have good beaches and reef?","a":"Yes — the country''s best mainland beaches on a 16-mile peninsula, plus the closest mainland launch to the southern reef. Splash Dive Center''s home waters — the Silk Cayes, South Water Caye and Laughing Bird Caye — are \"postcard perfect islands on the barrier reef\" with turtles, sharks, rays and eels, most a 30–60 minute run out.","source":"splashbelize.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"Can you fly-fish the flats in Placencia?","a":"Yes — the southern flats and river mouths are world-class permit water, fishable year-round for permit, bonefish and tarpon by skiff. It''s a high-value niche booked through Placencia fishing lodges and guides, and a reliable green-season lever when the reef days are between fronts.","source":"jmbelizetravel.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"ocean"},{"q":"Is there a destination spa / wellness stay in Placencia?","a":"Yes — Naïa Resort & Spa is built for it: a 224-acre private property with a mile of beach, a destination spa and a private-island couples retreat, strong on both romance and wellness. It''s the anchor for a quiet-beach reset paired with reef or river days.","source":"naiaresortandspa.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"wellness"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Placencia?","a":"Dive-chamber distance and open-water boat runs, not crime. The nearest recompression chamber is on Ambergris Caye (San Pedro), a meaningful distance north of the southern reef, so plan conservative profiles and no-fly windows; the run to Gladden Spit is ~90 minutes each way with early 6–7am departures. There is no full trauma center on the peninsula — serious cases evacuate to Belize City.","source":"ambergriscaye.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is swimming with whale sharks dangerous?","a":"It runs guided-only with a permitted operator — Gladden Spit is inside a marine reserve and only permitted operators may run the aggregation, no-touch and no-chase. Snorkelers work the surface aggregation over 2–3 hours (moderate swimming ability needed); divers descend to ~50–80 ft to meet the sharks and must be certified and guided.","source":"flowersvacationrentals.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Placencia, Belize Travel Guide 2026 — Whale Sharks, Beaches & Reef | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Plan Placencia: the Gladden Spit whale-shark season (Apr-May full moons), Silk Cayes & Monkey River, best mainland beaches, luxury & private-island resorts, clear safety guidance and dive-chamber facts.","slug":"placencia-belize","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-06","search_language":"en","local_keywords":["tiburon ballena Placencia Belice","temporada tiburon ballena Gladden Spit 2026","playas de Placencia","tour Monkey River Placencia","buceo Silk Cayes Placencia","resorts de lujo Placencia"],"hreflang":["en","es"],"attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-07-06","last_verified_basis":"source_verified","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/belize","read":"2026-08-20T14:53:57Z","source_updated":"2026-06-12T10:40:30+01:00"}]},"primary_keyword":["Placencia Belize travel guide","whale sharks Placencia","Placencia beaches"]},"booking":{"advisory_updated":"2026-08-20","advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"liveaboard","status":"live"},{"si":"expedition","status":"live"},{"si":"diveglobal","status":"future"},{"si":"ocean","status":"future"},{"si":"wildlife","status":"future"},{"si":"culture","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Itz''ana Resort & Residences","price_tier":"ultra","virtuoso":true,"earning":"on application / host-Virtuoso / SLH trade / Fora","mor_posture":true,"note":"beachfront + marina, Small Luxury Hotels of the World","source":"https://slh.com/hotels/itz''ana-resort-and-residences"},{"name":"Naia Resort & Spa","price_tier":"luxury","virtuoso":true,"earning":"host-agency / Virtuoso AOR","mor_posture":true,"note":"224-acre, mile of beach, destination spa; R&H + Wellness","source":"https://www.naiaresortandspa.com/"},{"name":"Turtle Inn (Coppola Hideaways)","price_tier":"ultra","virtuoso":true,"earning":"Coppola Hideaways trade / host-Virtuoso / Fora","mor_posture":true,"note":"Balinese-inspired thatched beach hideaway near village","source":"https://thecoppolahideaways.com/resort/turtle-inn"},{"name":"Gladden Private Island","price_tier":"ultra","virtuoso":false,"earning":"on application / host-Virtuoso / private-island trade","mor_posture":true,"note":"single-villa caye, helicopter transfer on 7+ nights, whale sharks off-island","source":"https://www.privateislandsonline.com/central-america/belize/gladden-private-island"},{"name":"Ray Caye Island Resort","price_tier":"ultra","virtuoso":false,"earning":"on application / host-Virtuoso / private-island trade","mor_posture":true,"note":"private island on edge of Gladden Spit & Silk Cayes reserves","source":"https://raycaye.com/"},{"name":"Copal Tree Lodge (Muy''Ono, Toledo)","price_tier":"luxury","virtuoso":false,"earning":"Muy''Ono trade / host-Virtuoso / Fora","mor_posture":true,"note":"rainforest all-inclusive luxury lodge near Punta Gorda","source":"https://etichotels.com/journal/top-10-sustainable-hotels-in-belize/"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"Placencia, Belize"},"geo":{"lat":16.5155,"lng":-88.3665},"orbit":[{"id":"ambergris-caye-belize","jewels":11,"si":["tropical","liveaboard","romance","expedition"]},{"id":"blue-hole-belize","jewels":8,"si":["liveaboard","expedition","tropical"]},{"id":"caye-caulker-belize","jewels":9,"si":["tropical","liveaboard","expedition","ocean","culinary"]},{"id":"hopkins-belize","jewels":8,"si":["tropical","expedition","culture"]},{"id":"san-ignacio-belize","jewels":13,"si":["expedition","culture","romance"]}],"orbit_country":[]}'::jsonb, 83),
  ('playa-del-carmen-mexico', '10S', 'Playa del Carmen', 'Mexico', 'Cenotes, Fifth Avenue and the Cozumel ferry', 'live', 'verified', 'venice', 'Quintana Roo (Cancún & Riviera Maya)', '{"romance","expedition","diveglobal","culture"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Quinta Avenida (Fifth Avenue) is a multi-km pedestrian dining/shopping/nightlife street parallel to the beach.","Cozumel reef wall is a 40-minute ferry away (Xcaret Xailing/Winjet/Ultramar, ~US$32 round trip).","Cenotes Chikin-Ha, Chaak Tun and Eden are within ~30 minutes for swim/snorkel/cavern dives.","Xcaret and Xplor eco-parks (14-line, 3.8 km zipline circuit) sit just outside town.","Best weather is November–March; May–October is hot, humid and rainy."],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"Hospiten Riviera Maya, Playa del Carmen (+52 984 159 2200); serious trauma escalates to Cancún","malaria":"none in tourist Quintana Roo","yellow_fever":"none required","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-20T14:49:02Z","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00","source_country":"mexico","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely","fcdo_zones":[{"name":"The city of Tijuana, in Baja California","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["airside transit through Tijuana airport","the Cross Border Xpress bridge linking the airport across the border","federal toll road 1D and the Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border"]},{"name":"The city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"The state of Chihuahua","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Chihuahua","the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez via federal toll road 45","federal toll road 45D between Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez","the Copper Canyon rail route and the towns immediately on it, including Creel","the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro","state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua"],"note":"The advisory also covers the areas south-west of road 45D."},{"name":"The state of Sinaloa","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán","road 32 between El Fuerte and Los Mochis","the 15D federal toll road running the length of the state","the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis and El Fuerte, and the towns immediately on it"]},{"name":"The state of Tamaulipas","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo via federal toll road 85D from Monterrey","federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad Victoria and Magueyes","the area of Tamaulipas south of those highways"]},{"name":"The state of Zacatecas","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"In Guanajuato: the areas south-west of road 45D","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D. (San Miguel de Allende and Guanajuato City sit outside this area.)"},{"name":"The state of Michoacán","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Morelia via federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43","toll road 48D between Morelia and its airport","the town of Pátzcuaro via toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips on Lake Pátzcuaro","Federal Highway 15D"]},{"name":"In Jalisco: the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the Colima border","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"Thirty-nine named municipalities, including Autlán de Navarro, Sayula, Tapalpa, Cocula and Villa Corona — the advisory lists each by name."},{"name":"In Jalisco: eleven northern municipalities","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"Bolaños, Chimaltitán, Colotlán, Hostotipaquillo, Huejúcar, Huequilla el Alto, Mezquitic, San Martín de Bolaños, Santa María de los Ángeles, Totatiche and Villa Guerrero."},{"name":"The state of Colima","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Manzanillo by sea, or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport","direct travel via road 200 from that airport to Manzanillo"]},{"name":"The state of Guerrero, including the city of Acapulco","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air"]},{"name":"Within 40km of the Guatemalan border, from the Pacific Coast up to and including the Gracias a Dios crossing","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"Federal Highway 199 between Rancho Nuevo, outside San Cristóbal de las Casas, and the Chancalá junction outside Palenque","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"The restriction is the highway segment, not the towns at either end."}]},"timing":{"peak":"Dec-Apr (dry season; highest rates, biggest crowds)","shoulder":"May-Jun & Nov (~30-40% off, good weather)","green":"Jun-mid-Oct (hurricane/low; cheapest)","sargassum_window":"Apr-Aug (Jun-Jul peak); Playa moderate risk with barrier program","fill_the_beds":"green/sargassum months pivot to cenote dives, Cozumel reef, Xcaret/Xplor parks, Fifth Avenue food+nightlife","fire_date":"peak campaigns open Aug-Sep; shoulder ~3-4 months out","event_peaks":["Christmas/New Year","Spring Break (Mar)","Semana Santa"],"booking_lead":"peak 3-4 months; shoulder 4-6 months"},"jewels":[{"name":"Cozumel reef wall (Palancar/Santa Rosa/Columbia)","si_tag":"Dive Globally","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"World-class drift-wall diving on the Mesoamerican Reef, 40 min by ferry.","bookable_category":"dive excursion / liveaboard","source":"https://www.viator.com/Playa-del-Carmen/Cozumel/day-trips-d5501-d632","timing":"Dec-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"diveglobal","blurb":"World-class drift-wall diving on the Mesoamerican Reef, 40 min by ferry.","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"Amstar excursion 12% or dive-operator affiliate","wells":["move","activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["diveglobal"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"destination","diveglobal":"primary","expedition":"destination","romance":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":12,"commission_pct_high":12,"commission_lane":["operator","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"Cenote cavern dive — Chikin-Ha / Dos Ojos","si_tag":"Dive Globally","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"Guided cavern dives with light beams and stalactites in the world''s longest cave system.","bookable_category":"cenote cavern dive (guide required)","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attractions-g150812-Activities-Playa_del_Carmen_Yucatan_Peninsula.html","timing":"Dec-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"diveglobal","blurb":"Guided cavern dives with light beams and stalactites in the world''s longest cave system.","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"DMC excursion 12% / affiliate 4-8%","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["diveglobal"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"destination","diveglobal":"primary","expedition":"destination","romance":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":4,"commission_pct_high":8,"commission_lane":["DMC","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"Xplor zipline + underground river","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"essential","hook":"Mexico''s largest zipline circuit — 14 lines over 3.8 km plus amphibious buggies.","bookable_category":"eco-park adventure","source":"https://blog.xcaret.com/en/welcome-to-playa-del-carmen-mexico/","timing":"Dec-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","blurb":"Mexico''s largest zipline circuit — 14 lines over 3.8 km plus amphibious buggies.","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"Xcaret Agents / affiliate; park entry pass-through","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"destination","diveglobal":"destination","expedition":"primary","romance":"destination"},"commission_lane":["affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Cobá + Tulum ruins day loop","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","tier":"essential","hook":"Cliff-top Tulum plus bikeable jungle pyramids at Cobá in one Maya day.","bookable_category":"guided cultural excursion","source":"https://www.amstardmc.com/en/destinations/mexico/tulum/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","blurb":"Cliff-top Tulum plus bikeable jungle pyramids at Cobá in one Maya day.","when":"year-round","commission":"Amstar 12%; ruin entry pass-through","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"primary","diveglobal":"destination","expedition":"destination","romance":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":12,"commission_pct_high":12,"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band"},{"name":"La Casa de la Playa (Grupo Xcaret)","si_tag":"Romance & Honeymoons","status":"live","tier":"ultra","hook":"AAA Five-Diamond luxury on the Xcaret estate with private park access.","bookable_category":"luxury all-inclusive resort","source":"https://www.travelagentcentral.com/your-business/grupo-xcaret-launches-xcaret-agents-pro-booking-tool","timing":"Dec-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","blurb":"AAA Five-Diamond luxury on the Xcaret estate with private park access.","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"Xcaret Agents Pro — 15% auto-paid at check-out","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["romance"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"destination","diveglobal":"destination","expedition":"destination","romance":"primary"},"commission_pct_low":15,"commission_pct_high":15,"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Playa del Carmen?","a":"Sargassum, weather and water — not violent crime against tourists. 2026 is a record-forecast sargassum year, but Playa is moderate risk thanks to active municipal cleanup and a 5-km double-barrier program, with landings in pulses. Drink bottled water, use repellent for dengue (peak May–Nov, no malaria), and note hurricane season runs June–November.","source":"deeparrival.com / cdc.gov, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Can I dive Cozumel and the cenotes from Playa del Carmen?","a":"Yes — Playa is the best mainland dive base for both. Cozumel''s drift-wall reef (Palancar, Santa Rosa, Columbia) is a 40-minute ferry away at ~US$32 round trip, and cenote cavern dives sit under 30 minutes inland. Cozumel walls are drift dives for a reputable operator; cenotes are guide-required and weather-independent.","source":"viator.com / tripadvisor.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"What is there to do on Fifth Avenue?","a":"Fifth Avenue (Quinta Avenida) is the Riviera Maya''s densest dining and nightlife strip — a multi-kilometre pedestrian street of tacos-to-rooftop bars parallel to the sand. It is the town''s social spine, best on a weekday evening before the crowds; guided food-and-rooftop crawls are the easy way to graze it.","source":"tripadvisor.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"entertainment","si_fold_note":"folded from the retired `nightlife` slug into Global Live Entertainment 2026-08-23; the content is kept, the retired slug is not"},{"q":"Are the Xcaret and Xplor parks worth it, especially for families?","a":"Yes — they are the region''s marquee eco-parks. Xcaret runs cenotes, underground rivers and Maya performances; Xplor has Mexico''s largest zipline circuit (14 lines over 3.8 km) plus amphibious buggies. Park admission (~US$85–110 at Xcaret) is pass-through, and both sit just outside town — a full family day out.","source":"blog.xcaret.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Can I visit Maya ruins from Playa del Carmen?","a":"Yes — it is the corridor''s best ruins base. Tulum''s cliff-top ruins and Cobá''s bikeable jungle pyramids pair in one day loop, and Chichén Itzá is a longer day trip; early morning (Nov/Feb) is best. Amstar and other DMCs run guided excursions, with ruin entry as a pass-through cost.","source":"amstardmc.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Where''s the best luxury for a honeymoon near Playa del Carmen?","a":"The Mayakoba estate and La Casa de la Playa. Mayakoba (Rosewood, Banyan Tree, Andaz) is a gated 595-acre lagoon estate of Virtuoso-affiliated flagships; La Casa de la Playa (Grupo Xcaret) is a 63-suite AAA Five-Diamond boutique ranked #1 Resort in Mexico for 2025. Both are ultra-tier honeymoon addresses on Playa''s doorstep.","source":"jetsetchristina.com / virtuoso.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Playa del Carmen?","a":"November–March is the dry, cooler high season (best weather, highest rates); May–October is hot, humid and rainy at the cheapest rates. The value sweet spots are the May–June and November shoulders at ~30–40% off, with November landing clear of sargassum and ahead of the holiday surge.","source":"machupicchu.org / travelswithelle.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"planning"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Playa del Carmen Travel Guide 2026 — Cenotes, Cozumel Diving & Fifth Avenue | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Plan Playa del Carmen: cenote diving, the 40-minute Cozumel reef ferry, Fifth Avenue nightlife, Xcaret parks, plus straight 2026 sargassum, safety and dive-chamber info.","slug":"playa-del-carmen-mexico","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-04","search_language":["en","es-MX"],"local_keywords":["qué hacer en Playa del Carmen","cenotes cerca de Playa del Carmen","ferry a Cozumel desde Playa del Carmen","mejor época para visitar Playa del Carmen 2026","sargazo Playa del Carmen 2026","buceo en cenotes Playa del Carmen","Quinta Avenida Playa del Carmen"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-07-04","last_verified_basis":"source_verified","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-20T14:49:02Z","source_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}]}},"booking":{"advisory_updated":"2026-08-20","advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"romance","status":"live"},{"si":"expedition","status":"live"},{"si":"diveglobal","status":"future"},{"si":"culture","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Rosewood Mayakoba","price_tier":"ultra","virtuoso":true,"earning":"on application / via host-Virtuoso","mor_posture":true,"source":"https://www.jetsetchristina.com/where-to-stay-in-mayakoba-mexico-rosewood-vs-fairmont-vs-andaz-vs-banyan-tree/"},{"name":"Banyan Tree Mayakoba","price_tier":"ultra","virtuoso":true,"earning":"on application / via host-Virtuoso","mor_posture":true,"source":"https://www.jetsetchristina.com/where-to-stay-in-mayakoba-mexico-rosewood-vs-fairmont-vs-andaz-vs-banyan-tree/"},{"name":"Andaz / Alila Mayakoba","price_tier":"ultra","virtuoso":true,"earning":"on application / via host-Virtuoso","mor_posture":true,"source":"https://www.jetsetchristina.com/where-to-stay-in-mayakoba-mexico-rosewood-vs-fairmont-vs-andaz-vs-banyan-tree/"},{"name":"Fairmont Mayakoba","price_tier":"luxury","virtuoso":false,"earning":"on application / host AOR","mor_posture":true,"source":"https://www.jetsetchristina.com/where-to-stay-in-mayakoba-mexico-rosewo